text:
maria: heads-up, opened a docs PR to add a NodeJS streaming example for Nebula3b embeddings and a short migration note for customers who previously used split+avg. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4839. Trying to make the snippet copy-pasteable for SDK v3 and add CI smoke tests.

jon: Nice. Can you add the published bench link instead of raw numbers? We had a follow-up last quarter where docs numbers drifted and caused confusion.

maria: Yep, plan is to link to s3://redwood-benchmarks/nebula3b/embed-long-inputs/ latest.csv and reference commit hash. I also added a tiny smoke test that runs the example against a 700-token fixture in the docs CI.

leo: For compatibility note: can we call out behavior with quantized on-prem runtimes? I think we saw subtle norm drift when using non-overlapping streaming segments with int8. @ash any quick guidance?

ash: Short answer: quantized on-prem can increase inter-shard variance due to per-shard attention truncation and quantization noise. Suggest recommending streaming with 64-token overlap or use the hosted model (which preserves full attention) when exact vector stability matters. I'll paste a short blurb for the model card.

rachel: Docs nit: the Node snippet should use the new method name `client.embeds.stream()` (we recently aliased). Make sure the snippet uses async iterators since that's what customers expect.

maria: Updated snippet to async iterator style. Posting full example below for review (to be used in model card):

```javascript
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });

async function streamEmbeddings(text, model='nebula3b-embed', chunkSize=256, overlap=64) {
  const tokens = tokenize(text);
  const embeddings = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < tokens.length; i += (chunkSize - overlap)) {
    const shard = detokenize(tokens.slice(i, i + chunkSize));
    for await (const part of client.embeds.stream({ model, input: shard })) {
      // part.embedding is an array - push or stitch as needed
      embeddings.push(part.embedding);
    }
  }
  return stitchEmbeddings(embeddings, overlap);
}
```

jon: small ask: use `chunkSize` camelCase to match our JS SDK naming. Also add a one-line comment about fallback to the hosted endpoint for customers on older on-prem stacks.

maria: fixed to `chunkSize` and added fallback comment.

leo: LGTM from docs. Two follow-ups before merge: 1) remove inline bench numbers (you already did) and 2) add the smoke test as a GitHub Action step that runs in preview builds.

maria: Added action YAML and smoke test file. CI preview link: https://deploy-preview.docs.redwood.ai/4839 (preview build succeeded)

docs-bot: deploy-preview available: https://deploy-preview.docs.redwood.ai/4839 :white_check_mark: 

ash: Approved from eng-ml after wording tweak. Note I added a short sentence: "For customers on quantized on-prem, consider overlap>=64 or use hosted variant to avoid cross-shard discontinuities."

rachel: Approved from SDK docs POV. Smoke test passed in preview. :rocket:

maria: Merging after CI completes. I'll also send a short internal Support note with repro steps for when customers report embedding drift. Filed follow-up issue: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/issues/1184

jon: Great. If we see repeated tickets we can consider a dedicated "Embedding streaming and continuity" doc page with interactive examples.

maria: Filed as roadmap item in the docs backlog. Thanks everyone.
